```suggestion
   if (!mongoc_collection_rename (coll, NULL, new_name, false, error)) {
```

Passing `coll->db` reports a use-after-free from ASAN. `coll->db` is freed, than overwritten by the `new_db` [argument here](https://github.com/mongodb/mongo-c-driver/blob/1a97d00d91e7251482ffa76c9b4e854a384d9ce9/src/libmongoc/src/mongoc/mongoc-collection.c#L3192).

Since `coll->db` is not publicly accessible, this may not be a concern for users. Though a possibly more robust solution is to check whether `coll->db == new_db` in `mongoc_collection_rename_with_opts`:
```c
      if (new_db && new_db != collection->db) {
         bson_free (collection->db);
         collection->db = bson_strdup (new_db);
      }
```

